Task label and context length in the DSpark confidence dump, on top of
vllm-apertus-dspark-kv-cost.patch (apply the confidence-verify, paper-scheduler,
draft-cut and kv-cost patches first).

VLLM_DSPARK_CONF_DUMP lines carry request ids only, so a dump cannot be split
by workload: the per-request draft-length study (docs/per-request-k.md) needs
the task each request came from, which a serving gateway would know. A request
that sends a task in its vllm_xargs ({"task": "chat"}; the bench client sends a
workload row's "vllm_xargs") gets it in its dump lines as "label", and every
line gets the request's context length ("ctx", tokens computed) for the KV-read
term of methods/dspark/scheduler/headroom_sim.py. Nothing changes without
VLLM_DSPARK_CONF_DUMP.
